  You will be provided with 1) a partial code base, 2) an issue statement explaining a problem to resolve, and 3) a patch addressing the issue.
 
  <issue>
  install_screen shouldn't add screen to the DOM
Calling `install_screen` should add the screen to `_install_screens` but it should not add it to the DOM.

Screens should only be added to the DOM explicitly with `push_screen` or `switch_screen`

App children should only contain the current screen
Currently the DOM will contain every Screen on the stack. This means that doing `app.query` considers all screens and may produce unexpected results. 

We should restrict queries to only the current screen.

I think the best way to do this would be for `App` to have a custom `NodeList` object which only ever contains the current screen.

Flesh out API reference for screens.
The screens API methods on App are a little too terse. Devs that read the API without the docs are making incorrect assumptions. We should flesh these out a little more. Particularily around the concept of installing and uninstalling screens,
  </issue>
  
